# Objective

Detect PowerShell process executions containing encoded-command arguments.

Encoded PowerShell can be used legitimately, but it is also an execution characteristic worth investigating because encoded commands can obscure the contents of a command from casual inspection.

DET-003 provides an endpoint detection signal that can be correlated with:

- Parent-process information
- PowerShell Script Block Logging
- Network activity
- Child-process execution
- User context
- Additional SOC detections

DET-003 does not treat encoded PowerShell as proof of malicious activity.

