# Parent-Process Analysis

Search:

```spl
index=* EventCode=1 "powershell"
| table _time host User ParentImage Image CommandLine
```

Parent-process context can help explain how PowerShell was launched.

The analyst should evaluate the complete execution chain rather than treating any individual parent process as automatically malicious.

---

# Script Block Analysis

When Event ID 4104 is available:

```spl
index=* EventCode=4104
```

Search around the detection timestamp and endpoint.

Script Block Logging can expose the PowerShell content that was executed and provide additional context beyond the process command line.

Correlation:

```text
Sysmon Event 1
Process Creation
       +
PowerShell 4104
Script Block
       |
       v
Improved Execution Context
```

---

# Network Analysis

Review Sysmon network connections:

```spl
index=* EventCode=3
```

Narrow by:

```text
host
time
process
```

when appropriate.

Network activity occurring near an encoded PowerShell execution can increase investigative significance.

---

# Child-Process Analysis

Review process creation around the detection:

```spl
index=* EventCode=1
```

Look for processes created shortly after the PowerShell execution.

Conceptually:

```text
Parent Process
      |
      v
powershell.exe
      |
      +---- Child Process
      |
      +---- Network Connection
      |
      +---- Additional Script
```

Unexpected follow-on activity can increase confidence that the PowerShell execution warrants escalation.

